# HAPI FHIR org.hl7.fhir.* 6.6.7 transitive CVEs
# -----------------------------------------------
# The org.hl7.fhir.* packages at version 6.6.7 are transitive dependencies of
# hapi-fhir-validation 8.6.6 and are tightly coupled to hapi-fhir core — attempting
# to upgrade them independently results in AbstractMethodError at runtime.
#
# The vulnerable packages we CAN upgrade (convertors, dstu2, dstu2016may, dstu3, r4b)
# are already overridden to 6.9.0 in pom.xml dependencyManagement.
# Remaining packages (model, support, utilities, r4, r5, validation) require a full
# hapi-fhir major version upgrade (to 9.x or a version that bundles 6.9.4+) to resolve.
#
# Exposure assessment (VEX):
# - CVE-2026-33180 (auth leak in redirects): not exposed — we do not use HAPI's
#   HTTP client redirect-following in any authenticated flow; all FHIR calls go
#   through our own Spring-managed HTTP stack.
# - CVE-2026-34359 (Authentication Credential Leakage via …): same rationale; no
#   FHIR server acting as HTTP client with credential-bearing outbound requests.
# - CVE-2026-34361 (FHIR Validator /loadIG SSRF): not exposed — we do not expose
#   HAPI's FHIR Validator HTTP service (/loadIG endpoint is not mounted).
# Risk: LOW. Tracked in issue (TODO: file issue) for the eventual HAPI 9.x upgrade.
CVE-2026-33180
CVE-2026-34359
CVE-2026-34361
